# Local model weights (GGUF, ~3.9 GB; not part of the memory subsystem)
models/

# Installed dependencies (type-check toolchain only)
node_modules/

# npm pack build artifacts (regenerable via `npm pack`; never commit)
*.tgz

# Plugin runtime artifacts. The plugin writes these into whatever workspace it
# is loaded into -- including this repository, when testing the plugin here --
# so they must not be committed.
#
# ANCHORED TO THE ROOT ON PURPOSE. A bare `memory/` matches a directory of that
# name at ANY depth, and this tree has a source directory called `memory`:
# `extensions/memory-core/src/memory/`. Under the bare rule, seven of its eight
# files were tracked and `manager-cpu-entrypoints.ts` was silently not -- an
# upstream file that happened to land in an ignored directory, invisible to
# `git status` and to every tool that walks the tracked tree. Nothing a rule
# meant to keep memory files out of commits should be able to do that, so the
# rule says `/memory/` and matches the root only.
#
# The workspace bootstrap names below share the intent and are already root-only,
# being file names rather than directory names.
/memory/
MEMORY.md
DREAMS.md
# Workspace bootstrap files the plugin reads/injects into the prompt;
# never ship them from a repo used as a workspace.
AGENTS.md
SOUL.md
IDENTITY.md
USER.md
BOOTSTRAP.md

# Real conversation data used as a retrieval test set. Personal, and specific to
# this machine's history rather than to the project.
training/

# Built memory-browser bundle (see scripts/build-web.mjs). Gitignored, but it
# ships in the tarball -- that is what .npmignore's `!web/dist` is for.
web/dist/

# Scratch output from local model / service experiments
serve-test.log
serve-test.err
*.log

# Transient probe scripts used to be listed one by one here -- probe-binding.mjs,
# diag.mjs, meta.mjs, raw.mjs, fewshot.mjs, t.mjs, t2.mjs, t3.mjs, m2.mjs, m3.mjs
# -- ten lines naming files that only ever existed in a working tree and were
# never committed (`git log --diff-filter=A` for all ten is empty). They are gone,
# and the list was a worse rule than no rule: it invited the next scratch script
# to be added by name, one more line, forever. A probe left next to the code now
# shows up as untracked, which is what untracked means.
#
# There is no blanket `*.txt` here either. The two .txt files that legitimately
# belong to this build are listed by name at the bottom; the only others in the
# tree were scratch output from one afternoon of probing.
# local dev notes (never publish)
TODO.md

VERIFY.md

# Windows installer build output. The payload dir holds the unpacked tarball that gets
# embedded (~2550 files), dist holds the installer; build.ps1 regenerates both.
# version.nsh and nsis-paths.nsh are written by the build (the version lives in
# package.json; the NSIS language path is machine-specific), so neither is hand-maintained.
# payload-manifest.nsh is likewise generated by build.ps1 from the tree it just staged --
# it is the explicit Delete/RMDir list the uninstaller runs, ~157 KB, and changes on every
# build that touches the payload. Committing it would only ever be a stale copy.
#
# payload-files.txt / payload-dirs.txt are its runtime counterparts, same origin and same
# reason. They are named rather than covered by a blanket extension rule on purpose: they are
# the lists one install writes into $INSTDIR for the next install to read back, so a committed
# copy would be a stale inventory of someone else's machine -- and a blanket rule that covers
# them is one nobody will read before tightening it into a rule that starts tracking two 80 KB
# build artifacts.
#
# payload-hashes.txt is the SHA-256 manifest generated from the same staged tree and embedded
# in the installer only; it is never written into $INSTDIR. It is generated for the same reason
# as the lists above.
installer/nsis/dist/
installer/nsis/payload/*
# No `.gitkeep` exception: there is no `.gitkeep`, and `build.ps1` creates the
# staging directory it needs. A negation for a file that does not exist reads as
# a decision ("the directory is kept in git") while doing nothing.
installer/nsis/version.nsh
installer/nsis/nsis-paths.nsh
installer/nsis/payload-manifest.nsh
installer/nsis/payload-files.txt
installer/nsis/payload-dirs.txt
installer/nsis/payload-hashes.txt
